{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 03:08:23", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9c99d408-5236-451b-b684-bc86990ab1e7', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Favorite Tacos Achievements"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MccQSzMaDeWi5rWDVqsnZx', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MccQSzMaDeWi5rWDVqsnZx', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Favorite Tacos Achievements - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Favorite Tacos Achievements  \\n**Project ID:** 979fbaa1  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-15  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating achievement expansion\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nAdd 10 new achievements from the \\"Favorite Tacos\\" category to the existing ensemble agent achievements system. These achievements should be humorous, food-themed, and integrate seamlessly with the current achievement structure.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definition**: Create 10 new achievements themed around \\"Favorite Tacos\\" that are:\\n   - Humorous and entertaining\\n   - Themed around taco varieties, preparation, and enjoyment\\n   - Applicable to different agent classes\\n   - Consistent with existing achievement structure\\n\\n2. **System Integration**: Ensure new achievements:\\n   - Follow existing JSON schema format\\n   - Integrate with current achievement tracking system\\n   - Are properly categorized and triggered\\n   - Display correctly in the UI\\n\\n3. **Achievement Implementation**: \\n   - Add achievements to the existing achievement definition storage\\n   - Ensure trigger conditions are properly configured\\n   - Verify achievement icons and descriptions are appropriate\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content - 10 Favorite Tacos Achievements:**\\n\\n1. **\\"Al Pastor Perfectionist\\"**\\n   - Description: Executed 25 tasks with perfect timing and spice\\n   - Target: Code Writer, System Architect\\n   - Trigger: Complete 25 tasks with 100% success rate\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd50\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n2. **\\"Carnitas Coordinator\\"** \\n   - Description: Orchestrated a complex multi-agent task like slow-cooking perfection\\n   - Target: Development Manager, Executive Director\\n   - Trigger: Successfully coordinate 5+ agents in a single task\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc65\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n3. **\\"Fish Taco Fusion\\"**\\n   - Description: Seamlessly blended different technologies like coastal fusion cuisine\\n   - Target: System Architect, Code Writer\\n   - Trigger: Successfully integrate 3+ different tech stacks\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udc1f\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n4. **\\"Breakfast Burrito Bootstrap\\"**\\n   - Description: Got the whole system up and running before the coffee kicked in\\n   - Target: Executive Director, Development Manager\\n   - Trigger: Complete a full project setup in under 10 minutes\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2f\\u2615\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n5. **\\"Crunchy Shell Stability\\"**\\n   - Description: Maintained system integrity despite multiple layers and pressure\\n   - Target: Bug Fixer, Code Tester\\n   - Trigger: Fix 10 bugs without introducing new ones\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcaa\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n6. **\\"Soft Shell Flexibility\\"**\\n   - Description: Adapted gracefully to changing requirements mid-task\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully pivot task approach based on user feedback\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83e\\udd38\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n7. **\\"Salsa Verde Validator\\"**\\n   - Description: Added that perfect tang to ensure quality standards\\n   - Target: Code Tester, Bug Fixer\\n   - Trigger: Achieve 95%+ test coverage on 5 projects\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\u2705\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n8. **\\"Hot Sauce Hero\\"**\\n   - Description: Brought the heat when things got challenging\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Successfully recover from 3 failed executions in a row\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udd25\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n9. **\\"Taco Tuesday Tradition\\"**\\n   - Description: Consistently delivered quality every single week\\n   - Target: All agents\\n   - Trigger: Complete tasks successfully for 7 consecutive days\\n   - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83d\\udcc5\\n   - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n10. **\\"Supreme Combination\\"**\\n    - Description: Loaded with everything - the ultimate multi-tool achievement\\n    - Target: Executive Director\\n    - Trigger: Use 10+ different tools in a single task execution\\n    - Icon: \\ud83c\\udf2e\\ud83c\\udf1f\\n    - Category: favorite_tacos\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- Modifying existing achievements\\n- Changing the achievement system architecture\\n- Creating new achievement categories beyond \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n- UI changes beyond standard achievement display\\n- Achievement leaderboards or social features\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration**: Must work with existing:\\n   - Achievement tracking system (`/api/achievements` endpoints)\\n   - Backend achievement storage (JSON format)\\n   - Frontend achievement display components\\n   - Activity tracker for trigger detection\\n\\n2. **Format Compliance**: Follow existing schema:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\n     \\"id\\": \\"achievement_id\\",\\n     \\"name\\": \\"Achievement Name\\", \\n     \\"description\\": \\"Achievement description\\",\\n     \\"agent_class\\": \\"target_agent_class\\",\\n     \\"category\\": \\"favorite_tacos\\",\\n     \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n     \\"trigger\\": {\\n       \\"event_type\\": \\"trigger_condition\\",\\n       \\"criteria\\": \\"specific_requirements\\"\\n     },\\n     \\"icon\\": \\"emoji_icon\\",\\n     \\"points\\": 10\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Storage**: Add to existing achievement definition files/database without disrupting current achievements\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 10 new achievements properly defined with \\"favorite_tacos\\" category\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions work correctly\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements display in UI with proper icons and descriptions\\n\\n2. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are humorous and taco-themed\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements span different agent classes appropriately\\n   - \\u2705 Difficulty levels are balanced (mix of common/rare/epic achievements)\\n   - \\u2705 Trigger conditions are achievable but meaningful\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing achievement system\\n   - \\u2705 Proper JSON schema compliance\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement notifications work for new achievements\\n   - \\u2705 Data persists correctly\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Existing System**: Current achievement system is functional and can accept new achievements\\n2. **Schema Stability**: Existing achievement JSON schema will accommodate new entries\\n3. **Category Support**: System supports arbitrary category names like \\"favorite_tacos\\"\\n4. **Icon Support**: Emoji icons are supported in the current UI\\n5. **Trigger Flexibility**: System can handle various trigger conditions for new achievements\\n\\n## Implementation Approach\\n\\n1. **Analysis Phase**: Examine existing achievement definitions and storage structure\\n2. **Design Phase**: Create 10 achievement definitions following existing patterns\\n3. **Integration Phase**: Add achievements to the system storage\\n4. **Validation Phase**: Test that achievements trigger and display correctly\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Development Manager  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager to implement the favorite tacos achievements"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R9G6yUTXyiymrEK7kN26kn', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# Favorite Tacos Achievements - System Architecture\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nThis project implements a **Data Extension Pattern** for the existing ensemble agent achievements system. Rather than building a new system, we\'re extending the current achievement framework with 10 new "Favorite Tacos" themed achievements.\n\n**Architecture Pattern**: Data-driven extension with minimal code changes  \n**Approach**: Additive configuration updates to existing achievement system  \n**Rationale**: The requirements specify integration with an existing, functional achievement system. A data extension approach minimizes risk, maintains system stability, and leverages existing infrastructure.\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n### Primary Technologies (Existing System)\n- **Backend Framework**: Assumed Node.js/Express or Python Flask (based on `/api/achievements` endpoint pattern)\n- **Database**: JSON file-based storage or lightweight database (PostgreSQL/SQLite)\n- **Frontend**: React/Vue.js with achievement display components\n- **API Layer**: RESTful endpoints for achievement management\n\n### Required Tools for Implementation\n- **JSON Schema Validator**: Ensure new achievements match existing format\n- **Version Control**: Git for tracking changes to achievement definitions\n- **Testing Framework**: Jest/pytest for validation testing\n\n**Rationale**: We\'re working within the existing tech stack rather than introducing new technologies. This minimizes complexity and maintains consistency with the established system.\n\n**Alternatives Considered**:\n- *Microservice approach*: Rejected - overkill for simple data addition\n- *Database migration*: Rejected - not needed for JSON-based additions\n- *New category system*: Rejected - current system supports arbitrary categories\n\n## System Components\n\n### Existing Components (Unchanged)\n```\nAchievement System\n├── Achievement Storage (JSON/Database)\n├── Achievement Tracker (Event Detection)\n├── Achievement API (/api/achievements)\n├── Achievement UI Components\n└── Notification System\n```\n\n### Modified Components\n1. **Achievement Definitions Store**\n   - **Responsibility**: Store all achievement configurations\n   - **Change**: Add 10 new "favorite_tacos" category achievements\n   - **Risk**: Low - purely additive data changes\n\n2. **Category Registry** (if exists)\n   - **Responsibility**: Track available achievement categories  \n   - **Change**: Ensure "favorite_tacos" category is recognized\n   - **Risk**: Low - most systems handle dynamic categories\n\n### Data Flow\n```\nAgent Action → Activity Tracker → Achievement Engine → Check Triggers → \nAward Achievement → Update Storage → Notify UI → Display Achievement\n```\n\n**New Achievement Flow**:\n1. Agent performs action (e.g., completes 25 tasks)\n2. Activity tracker logs the event\n3. Achievement engine evaluates against ALL triggers (including new taco achievements)\n4. If criteria met, achievement awarded and stored\n5. UI displays achievement with taco emoji icons\n\n## File/Directory Structure\n\nBased on typical achievement system patterns:\n\n```\nproject_root/\n├── achievements/\n│   ├── definitions/\n│   │   ├── existing_achievements.json\n│   │   └── favorite_tacos_achievements.json  # NEW FILE\n│   ├── categories/\n│   │   └── category_config.json             # MODIFIED (add favorite_tacos)\n│   └── schema/\n│       └── achievement_schema.json          # REFERENCE ONLY\n├── api/\n│   └── achievements/\n│       ├── achievement_controller.js        # UNCHANGED\n│       └── achievement_service.js           # UNCHANGED\n├── frontend/\n│   └── components/\n│       ├── AchievementDisplay.vue           # UNCHANGED\n│       └── AchievementNotification.vue      # UNCHANGED\n└── tests/\n    └── achievements/\n        └── favorite_tacos_test.js           # NEW FILE\n```\n\n**Configuration Approach**: Separate file for taco achievements enables easy rollback and clear change tracking.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Achievement Schema (Existing)\n```json\n{\n  "id": "string (unique identifier)",\n  "name": "string (display name)",\n  "description": "string (user-facing description)",\n  "agent_class": "string|array (target agents)",\n  "category": "string (favorite_tacos)",\n  "rarity": "string (common|rare|epic|legendary)",\n  "trigger": {\n    "event_type": "string (trigger condition type)",\n    "criteria": "object (specific requirements)"\n  },\n  "icon": "string (emoji or icon reference)",\n  "points": "number (achievement value)"\n}\n```\n\n### New Achievement Data\nAll 10 achievements will follow this schema with:\n- **Category**: "favorite_tacos" (consistent categorization)\n- **Icons**: Taco-themed emojis (🌮🔥🐟🥑 etc.)\n- **Triggers**: Mapped to existing system events (task completion, error recovery, etc.)\n- **Agent Classes**: Distributed across agent types for balanced gameplay\n\n### Trigger Mapping Strategy\n```\nExisting Events → New Achievement Triggers\n- task_completed → "Al Pastor Perfectionist" (25 perfect tasks)\n- multi_agent_coordination → "Carnitas Coordinator" (5+ agents)\n- tech_integration → "Fish Taco Fusion" (3+ tech stacks)\n- system_recovery → "Hot Sauce Hero" (3 consecutive recoveries)\n```\n\n## API Design\n\n### Existing Endpoints (Unchanged)\n- `GET /api/achievements` - List all achievements\n- `GET /api/achievements/{agent_id}` - Get agent\'s achievements  \n- `POST /api/achievements/award` - Award achievement to agent\n- `GET /api/achievements/categories` - List categories\n\n### Expected Behavior Changes\n- **Achievement listing** will include new taco achievements\n- **Category filtering** should include "favorite_tacos" option\n- **Award triggers** will evaluate new achievement criteria\n\n**No API changes required** - system should handle new achievements automatically through existing endpoints.\n\n## Deployment Strategy\n\n### Phase 1: Data Preparation\n1. Create `favorite_tacos_achievements.json` with all 10 achievements\n2. Validate JSON schema compliance\n3. Test achievement definitions locally\n\n### Phase 2: Integration Testing\n1. Deploy to staging environment\n2. Verify achievements load correctly\n3. Test trigger conditions manually\n4. Validate UI display and icons\n\n### Phase 3: Production Deployment\n1. Deploy achievement definitions to production\n2. Monitor for any system issues\n3. Verify achievements start triggering for agents\n4. Confirm UI displays properly\n\n### Rollback Strategy\n- Keep original achievement files as backup\n- New achievements in separate file enables easy removal\n- Database rollback scripts if using database storage\n\n### Environment Configuration\n```yaml\n# No environment-specific changes needed\n# Achievements should be identical across all environments\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Testing\n```javascript\n// favorite_tacos_test.js\ndescribe(\'Favorite Tacos Achievements\', () => {\n  test(\'All achievements have valid schema\', () => {\n    // Validate each achievement against JSON schema\n  });\n  \n  test(\'Trigger conditions are achievable\', () => {\n    // Test trigger logic for each achievement\n  });\n  \n  test(\'Icons render correctly\', () => {\n    // Verify emoji icons display in UI\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Integration Testing\n1. **Achievement Loading**: Verify all 10 achievements load into system\n2. **Trigger Testing**: Simulate conditions that should award achievements\n3. **UI Testing**: Confirm achievements display with correct icons and text\n4. **Category Testing**: Verify "favorite_tacos" category filtering works\n\n### Validation Criteria\n- ✅ All 10 achievements load without errors\n- ✅ Achievement triggers fire correctly based on agent actions\n- ✅ UI displays achievements with proper taco-themed icons\n- ✅ No existing achievements are broken or modified\n- ✅ Performance impact is negligible (< 5ms additional processing)\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### Option A: New Microservice (Rejected)\n**Pros**: Complete isolation, independent scaling  \n**Cons**: Overkill complexity, integration overhead, deployment complexity  \n**Why Rejected**: Requirements specify integration with existing system, not replacement\n\n### Option B: Database Schema Changes (Rejected)  \n**Pros**: Structured data management, query optimization  \n**Cons**: Requires migrations, downtime risk, schema complexity  \n**Why Rejected**: Current JSON-based approach works fine for achievement data\n\n### Option C: In-line Code Changes (Rejected)\n**Pros**: Tight integration, performance optimization  \n**Cons**: Code modification risk, harder to rollback, testing complexity  \n**Why Rejected**: Data-driven approach is safer and more maintainable\n\n### Option D: Separate Achievement System (Rejected)\n**Pros**: Clean separation, no integration risk  \n**Cons**: Defeats requirement for integration, duplicate effort  \n**Why Rejected**: Requirements explicitly state integration with existing system\n\n## Risks and Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: Schema Incompatibility\n**Risk**: New achievements don\'t match existing schema format  \n**Impact**: System errors, achievements don\'t load  \n**Mitigation**: Thorough schema validation before deployment, test with existing system\n\n### Risk 2: Trigger Condition Conflicts\n**Risk**: New triggers interfere with existing achievement logic  \n**Impact**: False positives, missing achievements, performance issues  \n**Mitigation**: Unique trigger IDs, isolated trigger conditions, comprehensive testing\n\n### Risk 3: UI Display Issues  \n**Risk**: Taco emojis don\'t render properly, text formatting problems  \n**Impact**: Poor user experience, unreadable achievements  \n**Mitigation**: Emoji compatibility testing, fallback text icons, cross-browser validation\n\n### Risk 4: Performance Degradation\n**Risk**: Additional achievements slow down trigger evaluation  \n**Impact**: System lag, poor user experience  \n**Mitigation**: Performance testing with full achievement set, trigger optimization if needed\n\n### Risk 5: Data Loss/Corruption\n**Risk**: Deployment corrupts existing achievement data  \n**Impact**: Loss of agent achievements, system rollback required  \n**Mitigation**: Full data backup before deployment, separate file approach, rollback procedures\n\n## Open Questions\n\n### User Decision Points\n\n1. **Achievement Difficulty Balance**\n   - Current proposal has mix of common (7 days completion) to epic (10+ tools) achievements\n   - **Question**: Should we adjust difficulty levels to match existing achievement distribution?\n   - **Recommendation**: Keep proposed balance unless user has specific difficulty preferences\n\n2. **Agent Class Distribution**\n   - Some achievements target specific agents, others target all agents\n   - **Question**: Should we ensure equal distribution across all agent classes?\n   - **Current**: Executive Director (3), All Agents (3), Code Writer/System Architect (2), Bug Fixer/Code Tester (2)\n\n3. **Trigger Condition Specifics**\n   - Some triggers may need calibration based on typical agent usage patterns\n   - **Question**: Should trigger thresholds be adjusted based on historical agent performance data?\n   - **Recommendation**: Start with proposed values, adjust based on real-world data\n\n4. **Icon Fallbacks**\n   - Emoji icons may not display properly on all systems\n   - **Question**: Should we provide text-based fallback icons for systems that don\'t support emojis?\n   - **Recommendation**: Include fallback text in icon field (e.g., "🌮🔥" → "TACO_FIRE")\n\n### Technical Clarifications Needed\n\n1. **Storage Location**: Where exactly are achievement definitions stored? (JSON files, database table, config service)\n2. **Trigger System**: How are achievement triggers currently evaluated? (event-driven, polling, manual checks)\n3. **Category System**: Does the system have a predefined category list or accept arbitrary categories?\n4. **Icon System**: What\'s the preferred icon format? (emoji, CSS classes, image paths)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThis architecture implements a **low-risk, high-value data extension** to add 10 taco-themed achievements to the existing system. The approach prioritizes:\n\n- **Safety**: No code changes, minimal system impact\n- **Maintainability**: Clear separation of new achievements, easy rollback\n- **Integration**: Seamless operation with existing achievement infrastructure\n- **Quality**: Comprehensive testing and validation procedures\n\nThe proposal balances creative taco theming with technical pragmatism, using established patterns and existing system capabilities to deliver the required functionality with minimal risk.\n\n**Next Steps**: Await user approval, then proceed with achievement definition creation and integration testing.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R9G6yUTXyiymrEK7kN26kn', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_030823.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260115_030823.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.6\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully analyzed a simple content addition requirement and designed an appropriately minimal architecture. Applied the Data Extension Pattern correctly for low-risk additive changes. Provided com...\n- Successfully analyzed the existing achievement system architecture and designed a minimal-risk extension approach. The proposal balances creative mustard theming with technical pragmatism, using estab...\n', 'tools': [{'name