{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 17:22:48", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-08a871d9-981e-435f-9af5-8715c4dffe90', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "fix_recovered_jobs_continuation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Hb51VUTrYx9yAMk6hMQ8uL', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Hb51VUTrYx9yAMk6hMQ8uL', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Fix Recovered Jobs Continuation Bug\\n\\n**Project ID**: 986ded22  \\n**Date**: 2026-01-15  \\n**Submitted via**: Web UI  \\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nRecovered jobs don\'t continue execution after being recovered from a stalled state. Based on the user\'s directive to \\"fix, don\'t analyze\\", this is a known bug requiring immediate implementation of a fix.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Fix the Recovery Continuation Bug**: Ensure that when jobs are recovered from stalled/failed states, they properly continue execution from where they left off\\n2. **Ensure Seamless Resumption**: Jobs should resume without losing context, progress, or data\\n3. **Validate the Fix**: Verify that recovered jobs complete successfully after resumption\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Fix the bug preventing recovered jobs from continuing execution\\n- Update recovery orchestration logic to properly resume job execution\\n- Ensure state persistence and context restoration for resumed jobs\\n- Implement proper continuation mechanisms in the recovery system\\n- Test the fix with actual recovery scenarios\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- General recovery system overhaul or redesign\\n- Performance optimization of recovery operations\\n- New recovery strategies or features\\n- UI enhancements for recovery monitoring\\n\\n## Technical Context\\n\\nFrom the codebase analysis, the system has:\\n- A comprehensive recovery system (`swarm_recovery.py`) with multiple recovery strategies\\n- Recovery orchestrator that detects stalled agents and queues them for recovery\\n- Multiple recovery strategies: retry, refactor agent, enhance prompt, escalate model, manual intervention\\n- Recovery queue processing with concurrent execution limits\\n- Agent state tracking and status management\\n\\nThe issue appears to be in the job continuation mechanism after recovery, not the detection or queuing of recovery tasks.\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Recovery Continuation Works**: Jobs that are recovered from stalled states successfully continue execution\\n2. **State Preservation**: Recovered jobs maintain their progress, context, and data from before the stall\\n3. **End-to-End Completion**: Recovered jobs complete their tasks successfully after resumption\\n4. **No Regression**: Existing recovery detection and queuing continues to work properly\\n\\n## Constraints\\n\\n- **Fix Only**: User specifically requested fix implementation, not analysis\\n- **Minimal Disruption**: Changes should not break existing recovery functionality\\n- **Backward Compatible**: Solution must work with existing job/agent structures\\n- **Production Ready**: Fix must be robust enough for immediate deployment\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- The recovery detection and queuing system is working correctly\\n- The issue is specifically in job continuation after recovery\\n- Jobs have sufficient state information stored to enable continuation\\n- The problem affects all types of jobs/agents in the recovery system\\n- This is a critical bug blocking productive use of the recovery system"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014GuinPM5LjLmXxF9Yy1DjN', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Fix Recovered Jobs Continuation Bug - Milestone Plan\n\n**Project**: fix_recovered_jobs_continuation  \n**Date**: 2026-01-15\n\n## Milestone Overview\n\nThis project has a single focused milestone to fix the bug preventing recovered jobs from continuing execution. Based on requirements specifying "fix, don\'t analyze", this is a targeted bug fix with minimal scope.\n\n## Milestone 1: Fix Recovery Continuation Bug\n\n### Objective\nFix the bug that prevents recovered jobs from continuing execution after being recovered from stalled states.\n\n### Duration Estimate\n1-2 days\n\n### Deliverables\n1. **Root Cause Analysis**: Quick analysis of recovery continuation flow\n2. **Bug Fix Implementation**: Code changes to enable proper job continuation\n3. **Recovery State Management**: Ensure proper state preservation and restoration\n4. **Integration Testing**: Verify fix works with existing recovery system\n5. **End-to-End Validation**: Test complete recovery-to-completion flow\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Recovered jobs successfully continue execution after recovery\n- [ ] Jobs maintain their context, progress, and data through recovery\n- [ ] Recovered jobs complete their tasks successfully\n- [ ] No regression in existing recovery detection/queuing functionality\n- [ ] All tests pass, including new recovery continuation tests\n\n### Dependencies\n- Access to existing swarm_recovery.py and related recovery system code\n- Understanding of current job state management\n- Test environment for recovery scenarios\n\n### Technical Approach\n1. **Investigate Current Flow**: Examine how jobs are currently handled post-recovery\n2. **Identify Gap**: Find where the continuation mechanism fails\n3. **Implement Fix**: Add proper job resumption logic after recovery\n4. **State Handling**: Ensure job state is properly preserved and restored\n5. **Testing**: Validate fix with realistic recovery scenarios\n\n### Risk Mitigation\n- **Regression Risk**: Comprehensive testing of existing recovery functionality\n- **State Corruption**: Careful handling of job state during recovery transitions\n- **Performance Impact**: Monitor recovery performance after changes\n\n## Project Completion Criteria\n\nThe project is complete when:\n1. All Milestone 1 deliverables are completed\n2. All acceptance criteria are met\n3. Code is committed to version control\n4. Documentation is updated if needed\n\n## Resource Requirements\n\n- **Backend Developer**: Fix recovery system code\n- **Test Developer**: Create and execute recovery continuation tests\n- **System Knowledge**: Understanding of current recovery architecture\n\nThis single milestone approach reflects the focused nature of this bug fix project.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014GuinPM5LjLmXxF9Yy1DjN', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_172126.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260115_172126.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018jyj8xop6pncjnKqGyrzCW', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_