{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 17:25:19", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-20493b41-5b38-42fc-9a15-307d7265b81e', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Foundation & Theme System Setup - Establish the core theming infrastructure and CSS variable system",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SuXXZcyTNkkznwXTGtniTd', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SuXXZcyTNkkznwXTGtniTd', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Color Scheme Dropdown - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level Design\\nThis feature implements a **Component-Based Architecture with Global State Management** pattern. The architecture centers around a React Context-based theme system that provides centralized theme management while maintaining component isolation and reusability.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Modified MVC with React Context\\n- **Model**: Theme definitions and user preferences (stored in context + localStorage)\\n- **View**: Theme dropdown component and theme-aware UI components  \\n- **Controller**: Theme context provider with theme switching logic\\n\\n**Rationale**: This approach provides clean separation of concerns, makes theming globally accessible, and maintains React best practices without over-engineering the solution.\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **React 18+**: Modern React with hooks for component state and context\\n- **TypeScript**: Type safety for theme definitions and component props\\n- **CSS Custom Properties (Variables)**: Native CSS theming solution for performance\\n- **React Context API**: Global theme state management\\n\\n### Styling Architecture  \\n- **CSS Modules**: Scoped styling with CSS variable integration\\n- **PostCSS**: CSS processing with custom property fallbacks\\n- **CSS Custom Properties**: Core theming mechanism\\n\\n### Testing & Quality\\n- **Jest + React Testing Library**: Unit and integration testing\\n- **TypeScript**: Compile-time type checking\\n- **ESLint + Prettier**: Code quality and consistency\\n\\n### Storage & Persistence\\n- **localStorage**: Theme preference persistence\\n- **JSON**: Simple serialization for theme settings\\n\\n**Why These Choices?**\\n- **CSS Variables over Styled-Components**: Better performance, smaller bundle, no runtime overhead\\n- **Context API over Redux**: Simpler for single-purpose state, no external dependencies\\n- **CSS Modules over inline styles**: Better developer experience, CSS tooling support\\n- **localStorage over cookies**: Larger storage, no server overhead, perfect for client-side preferences\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. ThemeProvider Context\\n**Responsibility**: Global theme state management and persistence\\n```typescript\\ninterface ThemeContextType {\\n  currentTheme: Theme;\\n  availableThemes: Theme[];\\n  setTheme: (themeId: string) => void;\\n  isLoading: boolean;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. ThemeDropdown Component  \\n**Responsibility**: User interface for theme selection\\n- Renders dropdown with theme options\\n- Handles user interactions\\n- Shows current theme selection\\n- Provides accessibility features\\n\\n### 3. Theme Definitions Module\\n**Responsibility**: Centralized theme configuration\\n- Theme objects with CSS variable mappings\\n- Type definitions for themes\\n- Theme validation logic\\n\\n### 4. Theme Hook (useTheme)\\n**Responsibility**: Component-level theme access\\n- Simplified theme context consumption\\n- Memoized theme values\\n- Theme switching utilities\\n\\n### 5. CSS Variable Manager\\n**Responsibility**: Dynamic CSS variable application\\n- Updates document root CSS variables\\n- Handles theme transitions\\n- Provides fallback values\\n\\n## Data Flow Diagram\\n\\n```\\nUser Interaction Flow:\\n[User] \\u2192 [ThemeDropdown] \\u2192 [ThemeProvider] \\u2192 [CSS Variables] \\u2192 [Global UI Update]\\n\\nInitialization Flow:\\n[App Start] \\u2192 [localStorage] \\u2192 [ThemeProvider] \\u2192 [CSS Variables] \\u2192 [Initial Theme]\\n\\nComponent Access Flow:\\n[Component] \\u2192 [useTheme Hook] \\u2192 [ThemeProvider] \\u2192 [Current Theme Data]\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Header/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Header.tsx                    # Modified to include ThemeDropdown\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Header.module.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeDropdown/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeDropdown.tsx         # Main dropdown component\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeDropdown.module.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeDropdown.test.tsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 contexts/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeContext.tsx                  # Theme provider and context\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useTheme.ts                       # Theme access hook\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useLocalStorage.ts                # Storage utility hook\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 themes/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 types.ts                          # Theme type definitions\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 definitions.ts                    # Theme configuration objects\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 variables.css                     # CSS custom properties\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 themeManager.ts                   # CSS variable manipulation\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 storage.ts                        # localStorage utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 globals.css                       # Global theme variables\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themes.css                        # Theme-specific variable sets\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Theme Interface\\n```typescript\\ninterface Theme {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  displayName: string;\\n  description?: string;\\n  variables: Record<string, string>;\\n  accessibility: {\\n    contrastRatio: number;\\n    isHighContrast: boolean;\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Theme Context State\\n```typescript\\ninterface ThemeState {\\n  currentTheme: Theme;\\n  availableThemes: Theme[];\\n  preferences: {\\n    savedThemeId: string | null;\\n    autoDetectSystem: boolean;\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### CSS Variables Structure\\n```css\\n:root {\\n  /* Background Colors */\\n  --color-bg-primary: #ffffff;\\n  --color-bg-secondary: #f5f5f5;\\n  --color-bg-elevated: #ffffff;\\n  \\n  /* Text Colors */\\n  --color-text-primary: #333333;\\n  --color-text-secondary: #666666;\\n  --color-text-muted: #999999;\\n  \\n  /* Interactive Elements */\\n  --color-primary: #007bff;\\n  --color-secondary: #6c757d;\\n  --color-success: #28a745;\\n  --color-danger: #dc3545;\\n  \\n  /* Borders & Dividers */\\n  --color-border: #e0e0e0;\\n  --color-divider: #f0f0f0;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n### Theme Context API\\n```typescript\\n// Theme switching\\nconst { setTheme, currentTheme } = useTheme();\\nsetTheme(\'dark\'); // Switches to dark theme\\n\\n// Theme information access\\nconst { availableThemes } = useTheme();\\nconst isDarkMode = currentTheme.id === \'dark\';\\n\\n// Theme loading state\\nconst { isLoading } = useTheme();\\n```\\n\\n### Component Integration\\n```typescript\\n// Any component can access theme\\nfunction MyComponent() {\\n  const { currentTheme } = useTheme();\\n  return <div className={styles.container}>Themed content</div>;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Development Environment\\n- **Hot Reload**: CSS variables update immediately during development\\n- **Dev Tools**: Theme debugging utilities in development mode\\n- **Type Checking**: TypeScript compilation with theme type validation\\n\\n### Production Build\\n- **CSS Optimization**: PostCSS processes theme variables for browser compatibility\\n- **Bundle Analysis**: Ensure theme system adds <5KB to bundle size\\n- **Tree Shaking**: Remove unused theme definitions\\n\\n### Deployment Process\\n1. **Build**: Standard React build process with theme compilation\\n2. **Testing**: Automated tests verify theme switching functionality\\n3. **Integration**: Deploy with existing header component updates\\n4. **Rollout**: Feature can be feature-flagged if needed\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n```javascript\\n// No special environment configuration needed\\n// Themes work in all standard React deployment environments\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **Theme Context**: Test theme switching, persistence, initial load\\n- **ThemeDropdown**: User interactions, accessibility, visual states\\n- **Theme Manager**: CSS variable updates, fallback handling\\n- **Hooks**: useTheme and useLocalStorage functionality\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **Header Integration**: Theme dropdown renders correctly in header\\n- **Global Application**: Theme changes apply to all components\\n- **Persistence**: localStorage integration works across sessions\\n- **Cross-Component**: Multiple components reflect theme changes\\n\\n### Accessibility Testing\\n- **Screen Readers**: Theme dropdown announces correctly\\n- **Keyboard Navigation**: Full keyboard control of dropdown\\n- **Color Contrast**: All themes meet WCAG AA standards\\n- **Focus Management**: Proper focus handling in dropdown\\n\\n### Performance Testing\\n- **Theme Switch Speed**: Measure time from selection to UI update (<200ms)\\n- **Bundle Size**: Verify minimal impact on build size\\n- **Memory Usage**: Ensure no memory leaks from theme switching\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### State Management Alternatives\\n1. **Redux/Zustand**: Rejected - overkill for single-feature state\\n2. **URL Parameters**: Rejected - themes shouldn\'t affect routing\\n3. **Global Variables**: Rejected - not React-idiomatic, harder to test\\n\\n### Styling Alternatives\\n1. **Styled-Components with ThemeProvider**: Rejected - larger bundle, runtime overhead\\n2. **SCSS Variables**: Rejected - not dynamic, requires recompilation\\n3. **Separate CSS Files**: Rejected - loading performance issues\\n4. **Inline Styles**: Rejected - poor performance, no CSS tooling\\n\\n### Storage Alternatives\\n1. **sessionStorage**: Rejected - doesn\'t persist between browser sessions\\n2. **Cookies**: Rejected - server overhead, size limitations\\n3. **IndexedDB**: Rejected - overkill for simple preference storage\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Technical Risks\\n1. **CSS Variable Browser Support**\\n   - Risk: Older browsers may not support CSS variables\\n   - Mitigation: PostCSS fallbacks, graceful degradation to default theme\\n\\n2. **Performance with Large Component Trees**\\n   - Risk: CSS variable changes might cause excessive repaints\\n   - Mitigation: Use `contain: layout style paint` CSS property, performance monitoring\\n\\n3. **Theme Conflicts with Existing Styles**\\n   - Risk: Existing hardcoded styles might conflict with themes\\n   - Mitigation: Audit existing CSS, gradual migration plan, fallback values\\n\\n### User Experience Risks\\n1. **Theme Flash on Initial Load**\\n   - Risk: Brief flash of default theme before saved theme loads\\n   - Mitigation: Inline critical CSS, load theme preference early\\n\\n2. **localStorage Unavailable**\\n   - Risk: Private browsing or storage limits prevent theme persistence\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful fallback to session-only theming\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (Week 1)\\n- Theme definitions and type system\\n- ThemeProvider context implementation\\n- CSS variable system setup\\n- Basic useTheme hook\\n\\n### Phase 2: UI Components (Week 2)\\n- ThemeDropdown component\\n- Header integration\\n- Accessibility implementation\\n- Basic styling for 3 themes\\n\\n### Phase 3: Polish & Testing (Week 3)\\n- localStorage persistence\\n- Error handling and fallbacks\\n- Comprehensive testing\\n- Performance optimization\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n### Technical Metrics\\n- \\u2705 Theme switching completes in <200ms\\n- \\u2705 Bundle size increase <5KB gzipped\\n- \\u2705 Zero accessibility violations in automated testing\\n- \\u2705 100% test coverage for theme system components\\n\\n### User Experience Metrics\\n- \\u2705 Dropdown responds to all interaction methods (mouse, keyboard, touch)\\n- \\u2705 Theme persists across browser sessions\\n- \\u2705 No visual glitches during theme transitions\\n- \\u2705 Header remains functional on all screen sizes\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n1. **System Theme Detection**: Should we add automatic dark/light mode detection based on user\'s OS preference in v2?\\n\\n2. **Theme Naming**: Do you prefer technical names (light/dark/high-contrast) or branded names (default/midnight/accessible)?\\n\\n3. **Header Placement**: Would you prefer the theme dropdown in the user menu or as a separate control in the header?\\n\\n4. **Transition Effects**: Should theme changes be instant or include a subtle fade transition?\\n\\nThese questions don\'t block implementation but would help optimize the user experience based on your preferences."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.4\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
