D implementation."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EvkouZijDYzPra27m4UQvK', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/test_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation & Theme System Setup - Establish the core theming infrastructure and CSS variable system', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EvkouZijDYzPra27m4UQvK', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "test_tasks_identified": 31, "coverage_goal": 85, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "message": "Comprehensive test strategy created for Foundation & Theme System Setup milestone. Identified 31 test tasks covering unit tests (6 modules), integration tests (3 areas), E2E tests (2 flows), accessibility tests (1 area), and error handling (2 categories). Focus on testing core theming infrastructure without UI components - theme definitions, context management, CSS variable system, and storage utilities. 85% overall coverage target with 95% for core theme logic."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0149NDRRgbZHNJciGDM795R5', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0149NDRRgbZHNJciGDM795R5', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Backend Tasks - Foundation & Theme System Setup\\n\\n## Milestone Overview\\nEstablish the core theming infrastructure and CSS variable system for the UI Color Scheme Dropdown feature.\\n\\n**Note**: This milestone is primarily frontend-focused. However, there are minimal backend considerations for future API integrations and potential user preference storage.\\n\\n## Task Breakdown\\n\\n### Task 1: API Foundation Setup\\n**Description**: Set up basic API structure to support future theme-related endpoints\\n**Priority**: Low\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Basic API server structure in place (FastAPI or Express)\\n- Health check endpoint functioning\\n- CORS configuration for frontend integration\\n- Basic error handling middleware\\n- Environment configuration setup\\n\\n**Technical Notes**:\\n- Use FastAPI (Python) or Express (Node.js) based on team preference\\n- Configure for JSON responses\\n- Set up basic logging\\n\\n### Task 2: User Preferences Data Model\\n**Description**: Design database schema for storing user theme preferences (future-proofing)\\n**Priority**: Low\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Database model/schema for user preferences defined\\n- Support for theme_id field (string)\\n- User identification mechanism (user_id or session_id)\\n- Migration scripts created (but not necessarily executed)\\n- Model validation implemented\\n\\n**Technical Notes**:\\n- PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy (Python) or Prisma (Node.js)\\n- Keep schema simple: user_id, theme_id, created_at, updated_at\\n- Consider both authenticated and anonymous users\\n\\n### Task 3: Theme Preferences API Endpoints\\n**Description**: Create REST endpoints for theme preference storage and retrieval\\n**Priority**: Low  \\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- GET /api/user/preferences endpoint\\n- PUT/PATCH /api/user/preferences endpoint  \\n- Proper HTTP status codes (200, 404, 400, 500)\\n- Request/response validation\\n- Basic authentication handling (token-based)\\n- Error responses with meaningful messages\\n\\n**Technical Notes**:\\n- RESTful design with JSON responses\\n- Validate theme_id against known themes\\n- Handle both authenticated and anonymous users (session-based)\\n- Return sensible defaults for new users\\n\\n### Task 4: Session Management for Anonymous Users\\n**Description**: Implement session-based preference storage for non-authenticated users\\n**Priority**: Low\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Dependencies**: Task 1\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Session middleware configured\\n- Session-based preference storage\\n- Session persistence across requests\\n- Cookie configuration for security\\n- Session cleanup mechanism\\n\\n**Technical Notes**:\\n- Use secure, httpOnly cookies\\n- Set appropriate session expiration\\n- Consider Redis for session storage in production\\n\\n### Task 5: API Documentation Setup\\n**Description**: Set up automated API documentation for theme-related endpoints\\n**Priority**: Low\\n**Complexity**: Simple\\n**Dependencies**: Task 3\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- OpenAPI/Swagger documentation generated\\n- All endpoints documented with examples\\n- Request/response schemas defined\\n- Interactive documentation UI accessible\\n- Documentation includes authentication requirements\\n\\n**Technical Notes**:\\n- FastAPI auto-generates OpenAPI docs\\n- For Express, use swagger-jsdoc and swagger-ui-express\\n- Include example requests and responses\\n\\n### Task 6: Environment Configuration\\n**Description**: Set up environment-specific configuration for theme system\\n**Priority**: Medium\\n**Complexity**: Simple  \\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Environment variables for database connection\\n- Configuration for session management\\n- CORS settings for different environments\\n- Logging configuration\\n- Default theme configuration\\n\\n**Technical Notes**:\\n- Use .env files for local development\\n- Separate configs for dev/staging/production\\n- Validate required environment variables on startup\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n### Backend Scope Clarification\\nSince this milestone focuses on \\"Foundation & Theme System Setup\\" and the primary implementation is frontend-based (CSS variables, React context), the backend tasks are intentionally minimal and forward-looking.\\n\\nThe core theme functionality will be handled entirely on the frontend using:\\n- CSS custom properties for theming\\n- React Context for state management  \\n- localStorage for persistence\\n\\n### Why Minimal Backend?\\n1. **Theme System is Client-Side**: CSS variables and theme switching don\'t require server interaction\\n2. **localStorage Sufficient**: For v1, client-side persistence meets all requirements\\n3. **Future-Proofing**: These backend tasks prepare for v2 features like:\\n   - Cross-device theme synchronization\\n   - User accounts with preferences\\n   - Analytics on theme usage\\n   - Admin theme management\\n\\n### Implementation Order\\n1. Start with Task 6 (Environment Configuration) - needed by all other tasks\\n2. Implement Task 1 (API Foundation) - establishes basic structure\\n3. Add Task 2 (Data Model) and Task 4 (Session Management) in parallel\\n4. Build Task 3 (API Endpoints) once foundation is ready\\n5. Finish with Task 5 (Documentation) - documents completed work\\n\\n### Testing Strategy\\n- Unit tests for all endpoint handlers\\n- Integration tests for preference storage/retrieval\\n- Test session management functionality\\n- Validate error handling and edge cases\\n- Test CORS and security configurations\\n\\n## Dependencies Between Tasks\\n```\\nTask 6 (Environment Config) \\u2192 Task 1 (API Foundation)\\nTask 1 \\u2192 Task 2 (Data Model)\\nTask 1 \\u2192 Task 4 (Session Management)  \\nTask 2 + Task 1 \\u2192 Task 3 (API Endpoints)\\nTask 3 \\u2192 Task 5 (Documentation)\\n```\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- All API endpoints respond correctly with proper status codes\\n- Session management works for anonymous users\\n- Database schema supports theme preferences\\n- API documentation is complete and accessible\\n- Environment configuration supports all deployment targets\\n- Zero security vulnerabilities in authentication/session handling\\n\\n## Notes for TDD Coordinator\\n- All backend tasks should be implemented using TDD methodology\\n- Write tests first for each endpoint and data model\\n- Focus on API contract testing - ensure responses match expected schemas\\n- Include integration tests that cover the full request/response cycle\\n- Test error conditions and edge cases thoroughly\\n- Validate security aspects like CORS, session security, and input validation"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I effectively managed the complete project lifecycle from requirements analysis through implementation coordination. Successfully executed all phases sequentially: milestone planning, architecture des...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'proj