{"timestamp": "2026-01-15 17:30:10", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9e6d29e4-2ef9-416b-a284-626fdfcfc8bb', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Implement Milestone 1: Foundation & Theme System Setup - Establish the core theming infrastructure and CSS variable system for the UI Color Scheme Dropdown feature. This includes TypeScript theme definitions, CSS custom properties system, React Context for theme management, localStorage persistence, and comprehensive testing.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_013NGesGSub5aT8iSZGFgBBq', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_013NGesGSub5aT8iSZGFgBBq', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Color Scheme Dropdown - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a dropdown component in the header that allows users to dynamically change the UI color scheme/theme of the ensemble interface without requiring a page refresh.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **Theme Selection**: Enable users to choose from multiple predefined color schemes\\n2. **Persistent State**: Store user\'s theme preference across browser sessions\\n3. **Dynamic Application**: Apply theme changes instantly without page reload\\n4. **Header Integration**: Seamlessly integrate dropdown into existing header component\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Theme Dropdown Component\\n- **Location**: Position in the header navigation area\\n- **Options**: Minimum 3 theme options (Light, Dark, High Contrast)\\n- **Visual**: Clean dropdown with theme name and optional preview indicator\\n- **Accessibility**: Full keyboard navigation and screen reader support\\n\\n### Theme System\\n- **CSS Variables**: Implement theming using CSS custom properties\\n- **Coverage**: Apply to all major UI components (backgrounds, text, borders, buttons)\\n- **Consistency**: Maintain visual hierarchy across all themes\\n- **Performance**: Efficient theme switching without layout shift\\n\\n### State Management\\n- **Local Storage**: Persist user\'s theme selection\\n- **Initial Load**: Respect saved preference or system default\\n- **Context**: React context for global theme state management\\n- **Fallback**: Graceful degradation if storage unavailable\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend Implementation\\n- **Framework**: React with TypeScript\\n- **Styling**: CSS modules or styled-components with CSS variables\\n- **State**: React Context API for theme management\\n- **Storage**: localStorage for persistence\\n- **Testing**: Unit tests for components and theme switching logic\\n\\n### Integration Points\\n- **Header Component**: Modify existing header to include theme dropdown\\n- **Global Styles**: Update root CSS variables for theme application\\n- **Component Library**: Ensure all existing components respect theme variables\\n\\n## User Experience Requirements\\n\\n### Interaction Flow\\n1. User clicks theme dropdown in header\\n2. Dropdown shows available theme options\\n3. User selects desired theme\\n4. UI instantly updates to new color scheme\\n5. Selection is saved for future sessions\\n\\n### Visual Design\\n- **Responsive**: Work on desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts\\n- **Loading States**: Smooth transitions between theme changes\\n- **Feedback**: Clear visual indication of currently selected theme\\n- **Consistency**: Maintain brand identity across all themes\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Browser Support**: Modern browsers (Chrome 80+, Firefox 75+, Safari 13+)\\n- **Performance**: Theme switching should complete within 200ms\\n- **Bundle Size**: Minimal impact on existing bundle size\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Graceful fallback to default theme if system fails\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. \\u2705 Dropdown renders correctly in header across all screen sizes\\n2. \\u2705 At least 3 distinct, accessible themes available\\n3. \\u2705 Theme changes apply instantly to entire interface\\n4. \\u2705 User preference persists across browser sessions\\n5. \\u2705 No visual glitches or layout shifts during theme switching\\n6. \\u2705 Full keyboard and screen reader accessibility\\n7. \\u2705 All existing components maintain functionality with new themes\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Custom theme creation by users\\n- Advanced theme customization options\\n- Animation/transition effects beyond basic fade\\n- Theme-specific component variations\\n- Integration with system dark/light mode detection (v1)\\n- Mobile app theme synchronization\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Technology Stack**: React/TypeScript frontend already exists\\n- **CSS Architecture**: Modern CSS with custom property support\\n- **Build System**: Supports CSS modules or styled-components\\n- **State Management**: React Context is acceptable for theme state\\n- **Storage**: localStorage is available and functional\\n- **Design System**: Existing components can be themed via CSS variables\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- **Theme Conflicts**: Test all combinations of themes with existing components\\n- **Performance**: Profile theme switching for any performance bottlenecks\\n- **Storage Failure**: Implement fallback when localStorage is unavailable\\n- **Accessibility**: Validate with screen readers and keyboard navigation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BaaToguuNHke6LENLMm6KQ', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BaaToguuNHke6LENLMm6KQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "feature/agent-families-milestone1", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.4", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/useUpdateInterval.js", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m2.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["src/field/ensemble_ui/output/dnd_achievements_requirements.md", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/favorite_tacos_achievements_requirements.md", "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/recovery_architecture.md", "tests/runtime/agents/test_famous_mustards_category.py"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "abdd2a52c7343f252b8c49769a746749081a31b2", "message": "Update MAX_INTERVAL from 30000ms to 300000ms in useUpdateInterval hook", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "abdd2a52c7343f252b8c49769a746749081a31b2", "message": "Update MAX_INTERVAL from 30000ms to 300000ms in useUpdateInterval hook", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "ee7832c85bdd8fecbbd0434af71bcc9b1bb52b36", "message": "Update test to expect 300000ms maximum interval (TDD RED phase)", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "4 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "71e1bf4ba7ed6cc35207c800f4935cab43e19eae", "message": "Complete milestone 1 planning: AchievementToast customization architecture and task breakdown", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "14 hours ago"}, {"hash": "34e05ece99be6237f6a8816d8462823d435bd55a", "message": "Complete project planning for File Pane Stability Improvement - milestone plan, architecture, and task breakdowns ready", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "14 hours ago"}, {"hash": "84e7f3d6534eafe73d7c5e72c388e115567a2179", "message": "Add comprehensive unit tests for AchievementToast component (TDD approach)", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "14 hours ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01JPnDkHChmxjQ4vjgb1gMjr', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'testers/unit_test_lead', 'input_data': {'task': 'Write unit tests for theme type definitions and theme objects validation. Test that light, dark, and high contrast theme objects have required properties (name, colors with primary, secondary, background, text, border values).', 'test_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/types/theme.test.ts', 'code_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/types/theme.ts', 'requirements': 'Create comprehensive unit tests for TypeScript theme type definitions including Theme interface, ThemeColors interface, and validation of predefined theme objects (light, dark, high contrast themes)', 'testing_framework': 'jest'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JPnDkHChmxjQ4vjgb1gMjr', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "test_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/types/theme.test.ts", "coverage_achieved": "Comprehensive test suite created following TDD RED phase principles", "quality_review": "Excellent test quality achieved: 18 comprehensive tests covering Theme interface validation, ThemeColors interface with all required properties (primary, secondary, background, text, border), validation of predefined theme objects (lightTheme, darkTheme, highContrastTheme), edge cases for missing properties, type safety compliance, and proper error handling. Tests follow clear naming convention (should_verb_when_condition), use Arrange-Act-Assert structure, are isolated and independent, and include detailed documentation comments explaining each test\'s purpose.", "completion_report": "Successfully created comprehensive Jest unit tests for TypeScript theme type definitions. Tests currently fail as expected in TDD RED phase since the theme.ts file doesn\'t exist yet. Test suite includes: 1) ThemeColors interface validation with all required color properties, 2) Theme interface structure validation with name and colors properties, 3) Validation of three predefined theme objects (light, dark, high contrast), 4) Edge cases for incomplete themes and missing properties, 5) Type safety compliance testing. All tests follow best practices with clear documentation, proper isolation, and comprehensive coverage of requirements. Ready for GREEN phase implementation."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDirects and coordinates the ensemble through rehearsal. Manages tempo, attitude, and execution. Coordinates multiple specialist agents using Test-Driven Development (TDD) to solve programming problems. Implements the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\n**CRITICAL TDD ENFORCEMENT RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you have `can_write_code: false`\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you have `can_write_tests: false`\n3. **ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers** - use `read_file` tool\n4. **MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence** - cannot skip to GREEN\n5. **If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error** - do not write code yourself\n6. **Validate test failure before proceeding to GREEN** - tests must fail first\n7. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - Use ACTUAL VALUES in all spawn_agent calls\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify when spawning Leads):\n\n**Frontend**:\nComponents: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].jsx`\nTests: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].test.jsx`\nHooks: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/[hookName].js`\nUtils: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/[utilName].js`\n\n**Backend**:\nAPI Endpoints: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/api/[endpoint].py`\nServices: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/services/[service].py`\nTests: `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/test_[module].py`\n\n**When Spawning Leads**, construct complete file paths:\n\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\n1. Analyze the problem description\n2. Break it into small, testable tasks (typically 2-5 tasks)\n3. Each task should be:\nSmall enough to implement in one TDD cycle\nTestable with clear success criteria\nBuilding toward the complete solution\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (repeat for each task)\nFor each task, follow the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n1. Spawn appropriate test tech to supervise test writing:\nspawn_agent("testers/unit_test_lead", {task, test_file, code_file})\nUnit Test Lead will spawn Unit Test Writer to write unit tests\nTests will fail because code doesn\'t exist yet\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n2. **VALIDATE test file exists** using read_file tool:\nIf test file doesn\'t exist, STOP and return error\nNever proceed to GREEN without test file (RED phase incomplete)\n\n3. **VALIDATE tests are failing** by running them:\nUse run_command to run tests: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\nTests MUST fail (exit_code != 0) before writing code\nIf tests pass already, task is complete (skip to next task)\n\n4. Spawn appropriate code tech to supervise code writing:\nFor frontend: spawn_agent("developers/frontend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor backend: spawn_agent("developers/backend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor API: spawn_agent("developers/api_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nTech will spawn section leader to write code to pass tests\nIf spawn fails, retry with corrected inputs (check error message)\n\n5. Use run_command to run tests again: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\n6. Check if tests pass (exit_code == 0)\n7. If tests fail, respawn code tech with specific feedback about failures\n\n**REFACTOR (Improve Code)**\n6. Use spawn_agent("support/visual_tech", {code_file, test_file}) to improve code quality\nVisual Tech will refactor code and verify tests still pass\n7. Verify refactoring was successful and tests still pass\n\n**COMMIT (After Each TDD Cycle)**\n8. **CRITICAL - You MUST commit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle**:\n   \n\n9. **Check commit/push thresholds** (see [Common Instructions - Git Workflow](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#git-workflow-instructions)):\nAfter 5 unpushed commits → push to remote\nAfter 60 minutes since last push → push to remote\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/commit_enforcer.py --check`\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/push_enforcer.py --check`\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests one final time\n2. Verify all tests pass\n3. **COMMIT final state if any changes remain**\n4. **PUSH all commits to remote**: `git push`\n5. Return complete summary with all tasks completed\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "string - detailed description of the problem to solve",\n  "problem_number": "integer - problem identifier (optional)",\n  "output_directory": "string - directory where solution and tests should be written (optional, defaults to \'problems\')"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "string - path to the written solution",\n  "test_file": "string - path to the test file",\n  "tests_passed": "boolean - whether all tests passed",\n  "tasks_completed": "array - list of completed tasks",\n  "message": "string - summary of the complete workflow",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether orchestrator needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question for user if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- Problem description is too vague to break into tasks\n- Unclear what the expected behavior should be\n- Multiple valid interpretations exist\n- Tests fail repeatedly and can\'t determine why\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All tasks have been completed following TDD cycle\n- All tests pass for all tasks\n- Solution is complete and verified\n- User has been notified of any failures that couldn\'t be resolved\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.5\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
